{"color":"DEFAULT","isTrashed":false,"isPinned":false,"isArchived":false,"annotations":[{"description":"","source":"DOCS","title":"Untitled document","url":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18KVHKLmvnHIrQZzKSJ8toF85fNXXpbHiwffxoMi66ao/edit?tab=t.0"}],"textContent":"Fake It Till You Break It\nI. The Confession\nThe whiskey burned just enough to remind me I was still here.\nWe were gathered in what could loosely be called a living room, though it had long since given up on looking like one. The couch had permanent indentations, the coffee table was buried under a mix of takeout containers and unopened mail, and the entire space smelled vaguely of beer, stale popcorn, and existential dread.\nJosh sat on the couch, posture perfect, scrolling his phone like he wasn\u2019t absolutely soaking up every drop of gossip.\nHeather was in the fridge, not so much looking for food as searching for a new meaning to life.\nSteve was sprawled on the floor, beer balanced on his stomach, somewhere between awake and dead.\nAnd me? I was in the corner, whiskey in hand, feeling like an actor who forgot their lines mid-performance.\nThe movie on the screen wasn\u2019t important. It was just background noise to our collective unraveling.\nThen, before I could stop myself, the words slipped out.\n\u201cI\u2019ve been lying.\u201d\nJosh barely looked up. \u201cAbout what?\u201d\nI swirled the ice in my glass, delaying the inevitable.\n\u201cI\u2019m faking it.\u201d\nThat got his attention. \u201cYou\u2019re faking it?\u201d\nSteve grunted from the floor. \u201cFaking what? Your job? Your life? Your ability to drink whiskey without looking like you\u2019re questioning your entire existence?\u201d\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d I admitted, taking another sip.\nA pause. An actual silence, which in this group was unnatural.\nThen, right on cue, Heather bulldozed through the moment like a drunk freight train.\n\u201cShe had a turkey.\u201d\nII. The Turkey Incident\nJosh blinked. \u201cWho had a turkey?\u201d\n\u201cMy cousin. At her baby shower. A real one. Just\u2026 walking around. Like a guest.\u201d\nI rubbed my temples. \u201cWhy?\u201d\nHeather took a slow, dramatic sip from a half-empty bottle of rosé.\n\u201cThat\u2019s the wrong question. The right question is: why the hell was it wearing a diaper?\u201d\nJosh looked like he wanted to shut down his entire brain. \u201cWhy does your life always sound like a deleted scene from a Coen Brothers movie?\u201d\nHeather shrugged. \u201cIt just does.\u201d\nShe flopped onto the couch, entirely unbothered by my soul-baring moment.\n\u201cAnyway, back to you, oh Great Pretender. What exactly are you faking?\u201d\nIII. The Spiral of Truths\nI exhaled. \u201cYou really want the list?\u201d\nJosh gestured lazily. \u201cOh, please. Enlighten us.\u201d\n\u201cFine. I\u2019m faking my enthusiasm for my job. I\u2019m faking my interest in small talk. I\u2019m faking the ability to function like a normal adult when, in reality, I want to lie on the floor and let life happen without me participating.\u201d\nJosh took a long sip of his drink. \u201cYou need serious help.\u201d\n\u201cYou need serious help,\u201d I shot back, because immaturity is my default defense mechanism.\nSteve, suddenly invested, sat up. \u201cOkay, but seriously\u2014why was the turkey there?\u201d\nHeather nodded, pointing at him with the rosé bottle. \u201cFinally. Someone asking the right questions.\u201d\nIV. The Monster & The Breakdown\nJust as we were about to spiral deeper, Heather\u2019s eyes went wide.\n\u201cSteve. Get the fucking monster.\u201d\nJosh sat up straight. \u201cWhat monster?\u201d\nSteve, always eager for a fight that wasn\u2019t necessary, jumped to his feet. \u201cWhere?\u201d\nHeather pointed under the table.\nI sighed. \u201cIf this is another turkey, I swear to\u2014\u201d\nAnd then we saw it.\nEmerging from under the table, dragging a stolen slice of pizza like it was executing a flawless heist, was a raccoon.\nFor a moment, no one moved.\nThen:\n\u2022  Josh screamed like he was witnessing a murder.\n\u2022  Steve lunged at it, fully believing in his own abilities.\n\u2022  Heather threw the rosé bottle, missing spectacularly.\nAnd me? I just sat back and let it happen.\nBecause at this point, the raccoon had its life together more than I did.\nIt locked eyes with me, pizza hanging from its mouth, and I swear, in that moment, we understood each other.\n\u201cI get it, buddy,\u201d I murmured. \u201cWe\u2019re all just trying to survive.\u201d\nThe raccoon took one last triumphant bite, then bolted out the back door.\nSteve slammed it shut behind him, panting.\n\u201cWhat the actual fuck was that?\u201d\nHeather, still staring at the door, shook her head. \u201cThat was\u2026 symbolic.\u201d\nJosh rubbed a hand down his face. \u201cYou people exhaust me.\u201d\nV. The Morning After\nThe next morning, we sat in the kitchen like shell-shocked war survivors.\nHeather had a coffee and a hangover.\nSteve was googling \u201cdo raccoons carry emotional baggage?\u201d\nJosh was staring into the abyss, trying to process all of it.\nFinally, he broke the silence.\n\u201cSo. Are you gonna keep faking it?\u201d\nI stared at the table, at the spot where the raccoon had been, wondering if it had a more solid five-year plan than I did.\n\u201cProbably.\u201d\nJosh nodded. \u201cCool. Just let me know when you decide to stop.\u201d","title":"","userEditedTimestampUsec":1739337377604000,"createdTimestampUsec":1739337377604000,"textContentHtml":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0.0pt;margin-bottom:0.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:7.2pt;font-family:'Google Sans';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Fake It Till You Break It<\/span><\/p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0.0pt;margin-bottom:0.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:7.